    "summary": "The PR updates the API Docker image to install `iputils-ping` and reworks `DeviceMonitoringService.PingDeviceAsync` to use the explicit `SendPingAsync(address, timeout, buffer, options, cancellationToken)` overload, adds a once-per-lifetime `PlatformNotSupportedException` warning guarded by `Interlocked.CompareExchange`, and moves the `iputils-ping`/CAP_NET_RAW guidance into the `PingException` log message. Reviewers should focus on whether the container change actually enables ICMP for .NET's managed `Ping` (raw sockets / capabilities) and on the now-honored cancellation token, whose exception lands in the generic catch and is reported as a ping failure.",
